WEBVTT

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.430
Which means...

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:12.690
Third Class Hisone Amakasu will officially
participate in the flight training.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.150
-She has been promoted.
-Where's Nao?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.860
My name is Hisone Amakasu.
Looking forward to working with you.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.610
At least you have manners.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.240
Yes! I will give it my best!

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.410
A rehearsal for the air show celebration
will be held this weekend,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.660
but joint training with the OTF
can be held at any time.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.370
Aww, seriously?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.670
Taking time away from ACM
will hurt us, won't it, Slope?

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.630
That's 'cause Castle and I just got here.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.130
What do you think, Long?
Is she on your radar?

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.970
Give me a break, Eel...

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.350
<i>Castle? Long? Eel?</i>

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.720
<i>Why English?</i>

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.770
<i>Are they all returnees from abroad?</i>

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:53.140
You know,

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.560
my phased array is normally solid
as a rock.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.400
But for some reason...

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.520
it doesn't make contact!

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.280
Is that what they mean?
I should be initiated in as a newcomer,

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.700
but it's just sexual harassment!

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.580
Oh no! Was that sexual harassment?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.740
No, you're safe!

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.580
Forest would always crack up
at those jokes.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.920
If Forest could handle it, then it's safe!

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.960
-Forest?
-She was a beauty that was like us.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.920
That's the TAC name of your predecessor,
Former First Lieutenant Moriyama.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.840
-Predecessor?
-The Dragon Pilot, three years ago.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.220
Your <i>senpai.</i>

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.390
Enough! Shut up!

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.520
<i>Senpai </i>Dragon Pilot?

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.940
DRAGON PILOT: Hisone &amp; Masotan

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.840
<i>Mambo Viking 01 FTCS.</i>

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.840
<i>The rear serpent is lagging.</i>

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.090
<i>Up the speed and catch up with the others.</i>

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.930
<i>You're too slow, Amakasu!</i>

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.560
Cutting 200 knots at 30,000 feet.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.850
You trying to stall us?!

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.520
Maybe, if you praised my flying skills
when I fly well--

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.770
<i>What'd you say?</i>

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.490
Not that one!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.540
<i>Oh, no. Zetton! Longtail!</i>

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.210
<i>Brakes! Hit the brakes!</i>

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.060
-That was risky.
-What a close call.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.320
<i>Cancel the training! Cancel!</i>

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.320
<i>What the hell was that, Amakasu?</i>
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.820
<i>I-I'm sorry!</i>

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.610
<i>But if you keep yelling,</i>
<i>I'll shrink and disappear--</i>

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.820
<i>What'd you say?</i>

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.490
<i>Oh... you heard that?</i>

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.500
<i>Your mic is hot, dumbass!</i>

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.870
The prospects are grim...

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.380
Oh, boy.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.630
I wonder if we can even practice
for the air show.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:54.380
<i>-</i>Wanna just go do the ACM, ourselves?
<i>-I don't have enough fuel.</i>

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.590
RTB immediately!

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.720
Amakasu, you come after.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.140
<i>God dammit!</i>

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.770
<i>Think of a TAC name, too!</i>

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.600
TAC name?

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.270
Oh yeah, Flight Leader Kakiyasu
mentioned that this morning.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.280
Masotan?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.360
Is there something wrong?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.250
Sorry, I don't understand you.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:29.750
I wonder if your old Dragon Pilot,
Moriyama, knows or did something.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.880
Ah! My suit!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.990
Wait a minute!

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.730
Nao, what are you up to?

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.570
GIFU AIR BASE AIR SHOW

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:37.440
Flight Leader Kakiyasu
mentioned that, this morning.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.530
But what does sewing have to do
with the air show?

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.620
Like, I'm gonna tell you.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.500
For OTF crew, who can't do anything
the day of the show,

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.750
we're supposed to do something,
within our power, to contribute!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:50.960
Oh, I see.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:54.250
Unfortunately, I became
an established Dragon Pilot.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:57.090
But Nao has found a spectacular way
to fill my void.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.050
I respect you.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.470
You... you're definitely my enemy!

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.720
Aww, why?

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.470
I was just assessing your value,
in comparison to me!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.350
What? Shut the hell up!

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.100
-What is this "standard value" crap?!
-Oh yeah, Nao,

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.150
did you know the former Dragon Pilot?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.320
-From three years ago.
-I don't know!

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.030
I don't give a damn about quitters!

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:21.820
-What about you, Okonogi?
-I was assigned here only last year.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.530
I see.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.580
Apparently,
they called her Forest Moriyama.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.170
You scared me!

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:34.000
Masotan?

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:39.380
Oh, I see. The TAC name
of the person before was Forest.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:45.260
I heard something at the briefing,
this morning, that got my attention.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.470
What is a TAC name?

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:52.230
It's something like an individual nickname
that each pilot has.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.600
A nickname.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:57.570
Usually, the higher-ups or your <i>senpai</i>
gives it to you, so you can't reject it.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:01.740
Oh, maybe Moriyama was called Forest
because it's part of her name.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.490
Moriyama.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:11.830
Forest.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.080
Amakasu!

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:21.840
How sad. Should I give you a TAC name?

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.720
Let's keep "kasu" from Amakasu,
so we can call you Crap!

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.510
Oh yeah, Forest.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:29.470
She had both these and these.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:31.770
No, that's not what I wanna know.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.350
-Where is she now?
-Three, two, one, break!

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.610
She quit at some point.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.270
-Huh?
-She didn't even say bye.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.280
When I was stationed at Tsuiki, I heard
a Gifu Dragon Pilot went on a flight

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.700
and never came back.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:45.990
So, does that mean--

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.570
High G Yo-Yo!

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.450
You're not Komatsu!

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.830
If you can't do this much,
the Gifu Air Show will be obsolete.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:53.830
Seriously?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.000
He's got the spirit!

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.830
As should of the flight launch leader!

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.500
Let's pull it off with one shot!

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:00.670
Yeah!

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:03.510
Bravissimo!

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.930
It melted through impressively.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.390
I'll go ahead with the data collection.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:11.180
Feel free to let it dissolve
as much as you want.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.520
I see you're still at 14 inches.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:20.690
Do you know someone
by the name Moriyama?

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:21.860
Moriyama?

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.900
They say she was a Dragon Pilot, here,
three years ago.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:30.160
That was a terribly unfortunate event.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.500
She was a testee
for my special prototype suits,

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.830
and I had made an especially
sensational design for her.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.040
It had cleanly and entirely melted off.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:42.840
You were referring to the--

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.840
Mr. Ikushima, what do you think?

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.390
I was hoping more than the arm
would move, too,

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.470
-but it is what it is.
-Thanks!

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.310
We'll line it with the battery...

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:58.270
<i>No one's interested</i>
<i>in the old Dragon Pilot.</i>

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.560
Just a single line! How impressive!

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:04.070
GIFU AIR BASE AIR SHOW

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.160
You don't have to push yourself to come.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.570
Another day is fine to meet her.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.750
All right.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.290
I'll see you on Sunday.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:23.250
Please, no personal calls in here.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:28.010
Constructing a harmonious relationship
with one's juniors is a justifiable act.

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.840
She's a civilian now.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:33.220
Junior-senior relations last a lifetime.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.850
She didn't have to quit.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.270
There should've been a way
for her to return.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:44.020
Her handling of transport aircraft
stood out, above the rest.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.440
What a waste of talent.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.120
Amakasu.

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:01.040
Forest.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:09.090
Just, who is that?

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:10.880
Moriyama...

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:15.470
<i>Hiso Maso.</i>

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:22.190
<i>Please, turn your attention</i>
<i>to the left field.</i>

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.770
<i>Now, the aircraft formation</i>
<i>of Gifu Air Base</i>

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:29.950
<i>and the "Aviation Meteor Shower."</i>
<i>Please, enjoy!</i>

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.790
<i>After their performance,</i>
<i>the formation will disperse</i>

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:40.870
<i>in preparation for the next program.</i>

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:47.300
What do you think?

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.550
This is my personal contribution.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.550
You couldn't do this, could ya?

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:58.600
Yeah. I'm jealous that you can
think of this as a contribution.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.430
Ouch!

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.480
Look, it's waving!

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.360
Pilot!

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.940
Mm-hmm, very good!

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.240
Oh my!

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:15.370
He sounds a bit on edge...

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:20.580
I wonder if she's related
to a crewman.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:21.580
Who?

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:25.420
Technical Sergeant Amakasu!
I need you to come with me.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:31.420
Blue Impulse isn't coming
to this year's air show.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.430
And Misawa's F-16 isn't coming, either.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.850
Which means, all eyes will be on Gifu.

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.100
And...

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:44.270
The last air maneuver in the program,
that Onaga put together,

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:48.570
was supposed to shock all the fans
from around the country, but--

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:49.610
But?

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.610
What Onaga hadn't expected,

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.860
was the engine to go out!

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.160
The other 15s aren't available,

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.540
and there are no extra ones
in maintenance.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.040
We have to cancel it.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.460
No! We can't let that happen.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:06.670
Why's that?

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:07.880
Because...

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:14.590
the plane failed after getting caught
in the OTF's slipstream, the other day,

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.630
or so we think.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:16.890
Huh?

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.470
It's the same plane we used in training.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.390
What?!

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.980
The OTF's slipstream is of a higher
temperature and pressure than normal,

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.520
which, most likely, damaged
the interior shaft.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.940
It's nothing but a miracle
that it didn't kill the engine.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.400
Could it be...

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:37.240
that's what Masotan
was trying to tell me?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.910
Um, in other words...

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.500
You're taking responsibility.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:46.790
Commander Sosoda?

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:47.710
No way!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.710
R-Responsibility?!

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.960
Don't worry, Amakasu.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:55.130
You can fly it.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.680
-What?
-I'm sorry.

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.720
-But--
-We're counting on you, Amakasu.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.930
-You can do it!
-Land those tricks!

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:03.640
You're the face of Gifu!

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:07.100
<i>I'm the face... of Gifu?</i>

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.940
I understand.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.320
I'm just a mere Dragon Pilot,

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:16.950
but I must rise to the occasion.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.070
I'll give you the best I've got!

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.450
As Gifu's representative... No.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.410
As the face of Gifu!

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.130
It's all over...

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:33.460
Gifu's dignity...

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.220
and the photo shoot with models,
after the flight...

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:39.720
I'm gonna pretend like I didn't hear that.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:44.010
He usually comes out
when I wear this suit...

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.600
This...

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.890
This is how it ends.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.270
Mama'll be sad.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:52.810
Here comes that accent of his.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:56.320
Came 'ere all da way from Kyushu, ya know!

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.610
She thunk I were gonna fly!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:03.200
Came all da way ter see me!

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:06.490
Unleashing your accent
and rattling on won't--

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.080
Oscar!

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:11.250
Oscar!

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:13.790
O-Oscar?

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.210
Good to see you again!

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.180
-Have you been well?
-Flight Leader Kakiyasu,

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.390
should she be in here?

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:24.720
It's fine. I called her.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:31.650
You were just trembling like a baby,
but now you're all better!

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:35.900
He always gets moody when there are
crowds of people, like today.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:39.030
I could hear him crying from Hangar 8.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.410
<i>The woman I saw earlier?</i>

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.530
Zaito, were you picking on him again?

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.870
You shouldn't do that.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.710
Um, excuse me, but do I know you?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:52.620
Oh, you're so funny.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.710
It's me!

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.590
Moriyama.

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:02.180
What?!

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:05.510
She was a former Dragon Pilot?

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:08.100
-You're kidding.
-That doesn't even look like her!

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:11.600
She's a mom through and through
to this little guy.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:15.020
Senpai, didn't you tell them?

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.480
Senpai?

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:18.820
She was my junior,
flying transport aircraft.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:22.610
I invited her because she wanted
to meet the new Dragon Pilot.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.610
So you're the Dragon Pilot, now?

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.200
Oh my gosh, you're straw thin!

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.280
S-So...

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:31.580
-you quit being a Dragon Pilot because--
-Mama!

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.290
I was pregnant.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:37.040
Pardon me, but it's about time...

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.670
I'd ride if I could,

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.420
but look at me!

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:44.220
There's no way I could!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:49.890
-Please.
-Huh?

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.930
If you know how to get him to swallow me,

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:54.770
then, please, teach me!

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.900
As my predecessor,
it is your duty to teach me!

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:02.740
And what's with "Oscar?"
Sounds too simple.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:05.820
He's got a name and it's Masotan!

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:08.280
And you, Masotan!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.660
How can you hate Otofu
and be okay with Oscar?!

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.580
And about Onaga's aircraft,

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:18.000
if only you had spelled things out for me,

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.420
I would've known how to--

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.670
Why?

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:24.340
Why, indeed.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:26.340
I dun git what's happening,

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:27.260
but he did it!

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.600
Great! To the mobile control!

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:30.970
There's no time!

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:34.180
We'll taxi the OTF directly out!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.100
-Let's get going, too.
-<i>Mrs. Moriyama!</i>

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:41.570
<i>Once this is over, will you create</i>
<i>a TAC name for me?</i>

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:43.110
Okay!

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.070
This may seem small,

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:50.330
but doesn't it look odd
without a pilot in the dummy cockpit?

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.080
<i>Thank you for your patience.</i>

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:55.580
<i>The final adjustments have been made,</i>

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.580
<i>and Gifu Air Base's F-15 Eagle</i>

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.420
<i>will arrive on the runway, shortly.</i>

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.470
Oh dear.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:11.220
<i>Our final program is presented</i>
<i>by the Air Development and Test Wing.</i>

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:14.600
<i>A maneuver aviation performance</i>
<i>by the F-15J.</i>

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:19.100
<i>We hope you'll enjoy</i>
<i>this stunning solo flight</i>

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:20.770
<i>by an experienced pilot.</i>

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:35.910
M-Masotan?

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.040
Huh?

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.880
The output is failing?

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:50.220
We've come this far, so let's just fly.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.350
I'll reward you with lots of food after!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:00.980
Would you do it for Mrs. Moriyama?

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.770
Only if it were Forest?!

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:09.900
<i>If you think I could bear your attachment</i>
<i>to my predecessor, then you're mistaken!</i>

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:15.660
Getting some blunt troublemaker to do this
was your choice!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.450
I said, I'd do it, so take responsibility!

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:24.710
You might think, talking about
your responsibilities isn't important,

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.710
but are you really okay with that?!

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:29.420
The output!

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:31.720
You might be fine with that,

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.720
but try visualizing what'll happen to me!

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.970
Looking dejected, in front of everyone.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:40.600
Just imagine the look I'd have on my face!

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:41.850
That sucks, right?

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.650
So please, Masotan,

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.280
fly for me!

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.000
Beautiful takeoff.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.970
Damn you!

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:16.390
Did the gears rise?

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.390
-They're in!
-And the flaps?

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.390
-They're returning, as normal!
-Yes!

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.030
Aren't they a little too into it?

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.320
I've never seen moves like that before.

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.740
Has Gifu been hiding this?

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:36.120
Such mobility, to this degree...

00:20:57.430 --> 00:20:59.680
I lied about the reason why I quit.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:03.940
It was actually because
Oscar wouldn't let me ride him anymore.

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:08.730
That's not a reason for giving up flying
and running off with a man.

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:11.320
Don't say it like that.

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:15.030
Are you still peeved at me
for stealing him?

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.820
Don't be ridiculous.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:19.530
I let you have him.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.410
Sweet.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:30.630
Senpai, how would you say the "kasu"
from Amakasu in English?

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:35.840
You really are simple.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.770
I don't like hearing that
from you, Persimmon.

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:52.070
Cheers!

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:55.860
I will now reveal Amakasu's TAC name!

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:57.820
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:03.620
Ta-da!

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.340
Ma... so... ta... n!

00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:24.470
My TAC name is...

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:27.270
Hisone!

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:28.810
Hi... so... ne!

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:35.030
Remember it, Masotan!

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:38.910
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:11.370
<i>You gonna do it or not?</i>

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:13.670
<i>Munch and gulp.</i>

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:15.170
<i>-La la la.</i>
<i>-There it is.</i>

00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:17.130
<i>-Is it slippery?</i>
<i>-No, it's not.</i>

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:20.510
<i>Sexy... jaguar!</i>

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:22.590
<i>It's, really, not slippery!</i>
